/*
 * Copyright 2026 NXP
 * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 *
 * System-PM constraint layer: mark which SoC power states stop this FREQME
 * measuring. Stacked on top of whatever the board target already applies, for the
 * system layer only (via EXTRA_DTC_OVERLAY_FILE).
 *
 * Every board target in platform_allow gets this list from its SoC dtsi, so this
 * restates what is already there. It is kept so the system layer does not depend on
 * those dtsi commits being in the tree: on a checkout without them, this is what
 * supplies the list.
 *
 * All three states are listed on every part. The block does not run in Power Down,
 * Deep Power Down gates the CORE domain and resets it, and in Deep Sleep whether a
 * measurement survives depends on the part and on the clocks selected: per MCX Nx4x
 * RM Rev. 6_RC2 Table 336 the FREQME row is Static in Deep Sleep.
 */

&freqme0 {
	zephyr,disabling-power-states = <&deepsleep &powerdown &deeppowerdown>;
};
